Positive Economics is neutral between ends: It avoids
economic value judgements. For example, a positive
economic theory might describe that manufacturing and
sale of cigarettes is injurious to health, but it does not
provide any instruction or judgement on what policy
ought to be followed to avoid cigarettes in an economy.
